♪ For you, oh, oh, oh

822
00:47:24,760 --> 00:47:27,320
♪ For you

823
00:47:28,560 --> 00:47:32,240
♪ For you ♪

824
00:47:33,800 --> 00:47:36,080
On Monday, the boycotts begin.

825
00:47:36,160 --> 00:47:38,920
Across Montgomery people refuse to use the buses

826
00:47:39,000 --> 00:47:41,000
as a response to Rosa's arrest.

827
00:47:42,000 --> 00:47:46,560
And in just over a year, on the 21st of December, 1956,

828
00:47:46,640 --> 00:47:49,720
segregation on buses in Montgomery was ended.

829
00:47:50,160 --> 00:47:51,480
So it all worked out for her.

830
00:47:51,560 --> 00:47:53,520
No, life's still hard for Rosa.

831
00:47:54,280 --> 00:47:56,360
She loses her job, so does her husband.

832
00:47:56,440 --> 00:47:59,720
It's a struggle. They keep fighting.

833
00:48:00,720 --> 00:48:03,520
And in June 1999,

834
00:48:03,640 --> 00:48:07,200
Rosa receives the Congressional Medal from President Clinton.

835
00:48:07,280 --> 00:48:09,680
The highest award given to any civilian,

836
00:48:09,760 --> 00:48:13,760
recognising her as a living icon for freedom.

837
00:48:14,320 --> 00:48:17,400
It took so long, though. Her whole life.

838
00:48:17,480 --> 00:48:18,880
Yes, it did.

839
00:48:20,560 --> 00:48:22,480
But she changed the world.

840
00:48:23,560 --> 00:48:26,800
In fact, she changed the universe.

841
00:48:27,520 --> 00:48:28,840
Look at this.

842
00:48:35,520 --> 00:48:38,160
Asteroid 284996.

843
00:48:38,840 --> 00:48:40,880
Also known as Rosaparks.

844
00:48:55,520 --> 00:48:56,680
♪ And we'll rise up

845
00:48:56,760 --> 00:48:58,760
♪ Rise like the waves

846
00:48:58,840 --> 00:49:00,840
♪ We'll rise up

847
00:49:00,920 --> 00:49:02,960
♪ In spite of the ache

848
00:49:03,040 --> 00:49:05,080
♪ We 'll rise up

849
